  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating skewness based on the proportion of probability assigned to unfavorable outcomes. It prefers the lottery with a greater portion of probability on unfavorable outcomes (i.e., more right-skewed). The individual, however, focused on the probability of avoiding a loss (i.e., the favorable outcome), which is the opposite of the skewness criterion. They preferred Lottery A because it has a higher probability of no loss (80% vs. 75%), which corresponds to less probability on unfavorable outcomes. This aligns with the less right-skewed lottery (Lottery A), whereas the reason would prefer the more right-skewed one (Lottery B). The individual did not mention skewness, the relative weight of unfavorable outcomes, or any consideration of distribution shape. Their justification is based on avoiding loss, not on the skewness of the distribution. Therefore, the decision reason was not used. The individual’s reasoning is inconsistent with the rule of the decision reason.",
